# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simulation output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything a run produces lands in runs/<name>/. It is regenerable, and it is
# big: the per-episode trade ledger is the bulk of it, and a single long run can
# be well over 100 MB (this working tree reached 1.9 GB across ~25 runs). The
# code and the configs are the repo; results are reproducible from them.
#
# To keep one result anyway -- a report is only a few KB and is worth committing
# when it backs a claim:
#
#     git add -f runs/main/report.md runs/main/metrics.jsonl runs/main/config.json
#
# Name the files rather than the directory. `git add -f runs/main/` overrides
# every rule below as well and will happily stage a 12 MB trades.csv with them.
runs/

# The same artefacts by name, so they stay ignored if output is ever written
# somewhere other than runs/, or if the line above is removed.
**/trades.jsonl
**/trades.csv
**/progress.json
**/progress.json.tmp
**/gui_config.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

.Python
build/
dist/
develop-eggs/
eggs/
.eggs/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
MANIFEST

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not written today -- agents are rebuilt from a seed rather than checkpointed --
# but torch artefacts have a way of appearing, and they should never be commits.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx

